  "name": "Mountain running uphill and trail, 8 weeks",
  "goal": "Train the uphill engine for mountain and trail running: steady steep climbing, hill repeats and power-hiking, pacing, and rolling terrain, with a taper.",
  "audience": "Healthy runners and hikers. With the handrail down the W1 walks at 6.0 km/h at most, so these sessions are power-hiking (for real running speeds see the running-mode plans, which need the handrail up); they train climbing strength and endurance, not running form or downhill, which need outdoor runs.",
